exports[`pnpm billing's output > applies alloplace, then verifies it 1`] = `
{
  "applied": {
    "code": 0,
    "err": "",
    "out": "alloplace billing.json v1 (eaa1ff9d2369) to https://demo.alloplace.com and Polar sandbox organization Test organization (org_test)

Postgres: the file is applied
Polar: 11 calls
  tag Meter "Voice minutes": tag it as LobbyStack's
  tag Meter "Alert SMS segments": tag it as LobbyStack's
  tag Meter "Call transfers": tag it as LobbyStack's
  create Product "Starter annual": 370.00 CAD a year, Voice minutes at 0.20 CAD each, Alert SMS segments at 0.02 CAD each, Call transfers at 0.02 CAD each; overage invoiced each month
  tag Product "Starter monthly": tag it as LobbyStack's; add 37.00 CAD a month; drop 30.00 CAD fixed
  create Product "Pro annual": 870.00 CAD a year, Voice minutes at 0.18 CAD each, Alert SMS segments at 0.02 CAD each, Call transfers at 0.02 CAD each; overage invoiced each month
  tag Product "Pro monthly": tag it as LobbyStack's; add 87.00 CAD a month; drop 100.00 CAD fixed
  detach Product "Starter monthly": detach "150 voice minutes a month", "50 alert SMS segments a month", "20 call transfers a month": the worker reports only each month's overage
  detach Product "Pro monthly": detach "500 voice minutes a month", "200 alert SMS segments a month", "100 call transfers a month": the worker reports only each month's overage
  archive Product "Starter annual": replaced by a product that invoices its overage each month; its subscribers keep it
  archive Product "Pro annual": replaced by a product that invoices its overage each month; its subscribers keep it
Links: 4 live prices of 2 sold plans, written once Polar sells what the file says

Polar:
  done tag Meter "Voice minutes": tag it as LobbyStack's
  done tag Meter "Alert SMS segments": tag it as LobbyStack's
  done tag Meter "Call transfers": tag it as LobbyStack's
  done create Product "Starter annual": 370.00 CAD a year, Voice minutes at 0.20 CAD each, Alert SMS segments at 0.02 CAD each, Call transfers at 0.02 CAD each; overage invoiced each month
  done tag Product "Starter monthly": tag it as LobbyStack's; add 37.00 CAD a month; drop 30.00 CAD fixed
  done create Product "Pro annual": 870.00 CAD a year, Voice minutes at 0.18 CAD each, Alert SMS segments at 0.02 CAD each, Call transfers at 0.02 CAD each; overage invoiced each month
  done tag Product "Pro monthly": tag it as LobbyStack's; add 87.00 CAD a month; drop 100.00 CAD fixed
  done detach Product "Starter monthly": detach "150 voice minutes a month", "50 alert SMS segments a month", "20 call transfers a month": the worker reports only each month's overage
  done detach Product "Pro monthly": detach "500 voice minutes a month", "200 alert SMS segments a month", "100 call transfers a month": the worker reports only each month's overage
  done archive Product "Starter annual": replaced by a product that invoices its overage each month; its subscribers keep it
  done archive Product "Pro annual": replaced by a product that invoices its overage each month; its subscribers keep it

Links: recorded 6 changes in run <uuid>.

alloplace billing.json v1 (eaa1ff9d2369) against Polar sandbox and https://demo.alloplace.com

File and Postgres
  ok     catalog eaa1ff9d2369 applied
  ok     the deployed code was built with this file
  ok     4 plans, 4 live prices
  ok     2 sold plans active and linked

File and Polar
  ok     currency CAD, one subscription per customer, plan changes on in the portal
  ok     3 meters
  ok     no Credits on the products: the worker reports only each month's overage
  ok     4 products, tagged and priced as the file says, annual ones invoicing overage each month
  ok     no discounts
  ok     webhook https://demo.alloplace.com/api/webhooks/polar, Raw, on, API version 2026-10
  ok     nothing else tagged for alloplace

Postgres and Polar
  ok     4 products linked, all live, tagged and priced as the rows say
  ok     Polar sandbox organization Test organization
  ok     webhook secrets match
  warn   product_vars: POLAR_STARTER_ANNUAL_PRODUCT_ID is product_0016, not the linked product product_0035. Checkout sells the linked product and ignores the variable, so remove it from the instance.
  warn   product_vars: POLAR_PRO_ANNUAL_PRODUCT_ID is product_0029, not the linked product product_0041. Checkout sells the linked product and ignores the variable, so remove it from the instance.
  info   product_vars: POLAR_STARTER_MONTHLY_PRODUCT_ID, POLAR_PRO_MONTHLY_PRODUCT_ID match their links and aren't needed any more; remove them from the instance when convenient.

